Aetiology of the cosmic safehold

    - here I look into the aetiology of the cosmic safehold, surveying the possible causes,
      reasons and other explanantia for its presence, seeking to explain it
        : re `cosmic safehold` see `^*Allan.+2026.+The presence throughout the cosmos` @ sources.brec
    - to begin with, the possibilities are obscure, but one thing stands out as obvious:
      the safehold is physically bound up (entangled) with the larger cosmos
    - now, already cosmology has looked into the aetiology of another such entangled phenomenon,
      the apparent fine tuning of the physical laws, constants and conditions of the cosmos
      for the support of life, and sought to explain *it*
        ∴ I begin by adapting the explanantia of that pre-existing aetiology by this procedure:

            for( each proposed explanans ⁠E⁠ of the apparent fine tuning ⁠F⁠ )
                ⁃ divorce ⁠E⁠ from the explanandum of ⁠F⁠
                    : note : that is all for fine tuning itself, it will not figure
                      as a premise of the present aetiology
                ⁃ apply ⁠E⁠ instead, mutatis mutandis, as an explanans of the cosmic safehold

        - the resulting set of adapted explanantia I then take to serve
          as the set of known, possible explanantia for the safehold
        - these I order by Jason Waller’s typologic scheme, as follows


                table, Typology of known, possible explanantia
                           for the cosmic safehold
                ╭╴                                           ╶╮

                  explain-  explanantic   name of explanans
                   able      ground

                    yes
                            necessity
                                          physical necessity

                                          supernatural design

                        ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈
                            contingency
                                          natural cosmogonal selection

                                          multiverse ensemble

                                          mundane design

                ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈
                    no
                                          null, brute fact


            : re `J.+W.+scheme` see `^*Waller.+2020.+Cosmological fine-tuning arguments` @ sources.brec :
             ‘The division goes like this.  Either the [phenomenon] has an explanation…
              or it does not.  If it does not, then the [phenomenon] is a brute fact. …
              [Otherwise] there is an explanation…  the explanation is either a necessary
              truth or it is not. … if it is not… then it must be [a] contingent [truth].
              This is the basic reasoning behind the classification scheme.’ §4, p. 201-2

    physical necessity

            • reality’s structure is explainable by a (yet unknown) theory of fundamental physics ⁠T⁠
            • necessarily ⁠T⁠ is true
            • ⁠T⁠ implies the safehold

        : see also `^*Friederich.+2026.+Fine-tuning` @ sources.brec :
         ‘a so-called *theory of everything* according to which… the laws and constants of physics…
          turn out to be dictated completely by fundamental general principles.’ §2.3
        : contra `^*Ratzsch.+and.+Koperski.+2023` @ sources.brec : that an explanans of this form gives
         ‘a promissory note rather than an explanation’ §4.1.2.1

    supernatural design

            • necessarily there exists a supernatural actor (God) who made and rules the universe
            • God made the safehold
            • God had reason to make the safehold

    natural cosmogonal selection

            • alternative paths of cosmogony are possible
            • our cosmogonal path is the product of a (yet unknown) natural process of selection ⁠P⁠
            • ⁠P⁠ promotes a cosmic safehold

        : see also `^*Friederich.+2026.+Fine-tuning` @ sources.brec :
         ‘a *dynamical* account of the generation of life-friendly conditions, in analogy
          to the… “dynamical” evolutionary account of biological fine-tuning’ §2.3

    multiverse ensemble
        : privately note : here the principal added premise is a necessarily tight coupling between
          a cosmos’s habitability and safeholding capacity, the universal structure of reality being
          such that the set of cosmic properties necessary for the former will in most cases (in most
          combinations of their permitted values) happen also to suffice for the latter
            : cf. `^*-.+the claim: hardly could life exist absent a speed limit on causation$`
              @ ._/01.tale-of-logic_form/._/60.vetting_their_explanantia.notes.brec

    mundane design
        : privately see `^^authorial priority$`i @ ._/text.notes.brec

    brute fact \ the null explanans
